# Supabase SSR & Middleware

## Clients

- Browser: `createBrowserClient` from `@supabase/ssr` with anon key only.
- Server Components / Route Handlers / Server Actions: `createServerClient` with cookie get/set/remove.
- Middleware: `createServerClient` that can refresh the session and write cookies on the response.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — service role or localStorage-only session in the app
createClient(url, process.env.SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY!)

// ✅ GOOD — SSR cookie session with anon key
createServerClient(url, anonKey, { cookies: { getAll, setAll } })
```

## Middleware

- Run auth session refresh on matched routes.
- Redirect unauthenticated users away from private routes (e.g. dashboard).
- Do not put secrets or service_role usage in middleware.

## Cookies

- Session must live in cookies so Server Components and middleware share the same auth state.
- Prefer cookie adapters from `@supabase/ssr` docs for Next.js App Router.
